From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mecid <mecidi.cc@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:20:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] plat/cix: sky1: BL2 platform support

CIX publishes TF-A for Sky1 without the BL2 platform files its makefiles
list.  Add them, written from the behaviour of the CIX BL2 the boot ROM
loads (v2.7-33527c31abbe):

* sky1_bl2_el3_setup.c: console, delay timer, boot flash, BL2 version
  string for UEFI, watchdog; MMU with the SE key-management page and the
  non-secure DRAM the SE reports; TZC-400 setup before BL31 is loaded;
  boot timing records; BL2 RAM log for UEFI's RamLogDumpDxe.
* cix_io_storage.c: xSPI and SPI NOR (read command from the bootloader1
  flash table), the two FIPs located through the cix_package_tool
  firmware header, image policies including NON_TRUSTED_KEY_CERT_ID;
  btcfg_get_value() and cix_bl_mode_is_backdoor() used by io_fip.c.
* cix_image_load.c, cix_bl2_mem_params_desc.c: BL31, OP-TEE and BL33 at
  the addresses and with the entry attributes of the CIX BL2.
* sky1_trusted_boot.c, sky1_rotpk.S: the root of trust is the hash of
  ROT_KEY built into BL2; NV counters read 0 (as in the CIX BL2).
* cix_cot_bl2.c: the TBBR chain of trust with the CIX split root: the
  bootloader2 trusted key certificate carries the trusted world key, the
  bootloader3 one (NON_TRUSTED_KEY_CERT_ID) the non-trusted world key.
  Unlike the CIX BL2, both are verified.
* platform.mk: mbed TLS for crypto (the CIX crypto-engine library is not
  public) and the ROT_KEY hash.

Not reproduced: bootloader3 recovery from a backup copy (needs flash
regions no current layout has) and boot progress codes.
